    <DataNode elementId="AT5G66040-MONOMER" textLabel="sulfurtransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q39129" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The STR16 protein has a single rhodanese domain and has some activity with thiosulfate &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [12482606]|. However, based on the low K&lt;sub&gt;cat&lt;/sub&gt;/K&lt;sub&gt;m&lt;/sub&gt; ratio observed with thiosulfate (0.5), it is likely that STR16 acts on another substrate &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt;. It was also tested with 3-mercaptopyruvate, but it shows almost no activity with this substrate |CITS: [12482606]|. Although the rhodanese domain has some structural similarity to the catalytic domain of Cdc25 phosphatases, STR16 does not have any phosphatase activity against the artificial substrate 3-O-methylfluorescein phosphate &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [17408957]|. Expression of the STR16 transcript levels increase continuously as the Arabidopsis plants develop and age |CITS: [17408957]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G66040-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G66040.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q39129" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12701" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G66040.1" />
      <Property key="EnzymeNotUsedIn" value="PWY-5350" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G66040" />
