    <DataNode elementId="AT1G79230-MONOMER" textLabel="Thiosulfate/3-mercaptopyruvate sulfurtransferase 1, mitochondrial" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O64530" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The ST1 enzyme has two rhodanese domains and can use two substrates, 3-mercaptopyruvate and thiosulfate, &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt;. In general, the enzymatic activity (kcat) is higher with 3-mercaptopyruvate, but the Km is lower for thiosulfate |CITS: [12437129][10601861]|. Additional enzymatic activity assays indicate that this protein is most likely acting on 3-mercaptopyruvate because it has much higher activity &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; with this substrate (K&lt;sub&gt;cat&lt;/sub&gt;/K&lt;sub&gt;m&lt;/sub&gt; = 14.6) than with thiosulfate (K&lt;sub&gt;cat&lt;/sub&gt;/K&lt;sub&gt;m&lt;/sub&gt; = 4.3) |CITS: [12482606]|. Notably, there is no evidence that ST1 levels or activity are induced by cyanide and there is no experimental support for the role of ST1 in cyanide detoxification to date |CITS: [12721843]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G79230-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G79230.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O64530" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AtMST1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Rhodanese homolog protein 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="AtRDH1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="Sulfurtransferase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_5" value="AtStr1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-4169, RXN-4168" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G79230.1" />
