    <DataNode elementId="AT5G66170-MONOMER" textLabel="thiosulfate sulfurtransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q2V2U4" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The STR18 protein has a single rhodanese domain and shows a high degree of activity with thiosulfate &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; (K&lt;sub&gt;cat&lt;/sub&gt;/K&lt;sub&gt;m&lt;/sub&gt; = 9.7) |CITS: [12482606]|. It also has very weak activity with 3-mercaptopyruvate, but this is not considered to be physiologically relevant |CITS: [12482606]|. Although the rhodanese domain has some structural similarity to the catalytic domain of Cdc25 phosphatases, STR18 does not have any phosphatase activity against the artificial substrate 3-O-methylfluorescein phosphate &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [17408957]|. Expression of the STR18 transcripts can only be detected in five to six week-old plants, similar to senescence-associated genes |CITS: [17408957]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G66170-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G66170.2" />
